     "<div>Hi everyone, </div><div>I have an issue when SWATbuildR tries to connect channel network. </div><div>This is the error on R : </div><div><br></div><div>\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium;margin:0px;word-break:break-all;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:16px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;margin:0px\">Analyzing connectivity of water object network...\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;margin:0px;color:rgb(204,0,0)\">  ✘ </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;margin:0px\"> 23 channel segments identified not connected to other channels or reservoirs.\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  ✔ </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;margin:0px\"> No disconnected reservoirs identified.\r\n\r\n</span><span></span><div style=\"overflow:hidden;padding:6px 0px 6px 10px;white-space:pre-line;background-color:rgb(230,230,230);display:block;border-left:2px solid rgb(153,23,23)\"><div style=\"display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;padding-left:6px\"><span></span><span style=\"background:unset;background-blend-mode:unset;border:unset;border-radius:unset;vertical-align:unset;break-inside:unset;clear:unset;display:unset;float:unset;isolation:unset;break-after:unset;break-before:unset;overflow:unset;zoom:unset;column-fill:unset;column-span:unset;column-rule:unset;columns:unset;mix-blend-mode:unset;opacity:unset;font:unset;font-synthesis:unset;image-orientation:unset;text-orientation:unset;writing-mode:unset;border-collapse:unset;caption-side:unset;empty-cells:unset;border-spacing:unset;line-break:unset;text-align:unset;text-align-last:unset;text-autospace:unset;text-combine-upright:unset;text-justify:unset;text-transform:unset;text-underline-position:unset;white-space:unset;word-break:unset;color:unset;letter-spacing:unset;text-emphasis:unset;text-indent:unset;word-spacing:unset;list-style:unset;quotes:unset;margin:unset;outline:unset;padding:unset;box-sizing:unset;object-fit:unset;object-position:unset;max-height:unset;max-width:unset;min-height:unset;min-height:unset;min-width:unset;width:unset;table-layout:unset;text-decoration:unset;text-overflow:unset;ime-mode:unset\"><span>Erreur dans check_cha_res_connectivity(data_path, id_cha_out, id_res_out) : \r\n\r\nConnectivity issues for the water objects identified!\r\n\r\nWriting the layer water_connectivity_issues.gpkg into &#39;../../Temp/buildr_project/Mini_CREATE/data/vector&#39;\r\n\r\nLoad the .gpkg layer in a GIS to analyze the features that cause issues. \r\nFix the issues in the land and channel layers before proceeding with the model setup.</span></span></div></div></span></span>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>On QGIS, the channel starting point and end point are generated in the wrong direction. And unless, we took care about the line stream network direction are correctly oriented from upstream to downstream. You can find the screenshot of my basin : </div><div><br></div><div><img alt=\"Capture_Error1.png\" width=\"566px\" height=\"251px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/R-SWAT/attach/1de225decb005/Capture_Error1.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\"><img alt=\"Capture_Error2.png\" width=\"566px\" height=\"259px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/R-SWAT/attach/1de225decb005/Capture_Error2.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance for your help. </div><div><br></div><div>Léna Fouque</div><div>Toulouse University</div>"
